You may have fooled these
idiots, but I'm not convinced.

260
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:09,500
You pull anything, and I'll
personally kick you out.

261
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,500
All right.

262
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,113
I'll keep that in mind.

263
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,054
Oh, I just remembered.

264
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:18,599
I brought along some of
Crocodile's jewelry with me.

265
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,997
Wow, I love you, sister.

266
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,021
You're the best.

267
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,376
Oh, boy, here we go.

268
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:25,921
Nami's been had.

269
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,560
It's Chick's bad news.

270
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,565
She's following her lead
like some kind of pet.

271
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,300
Oh, love. Bold.

272
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,617
The likes of which I've never seen.

273
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:39,420
I'm captured by your spell.

274
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,440
Held prisoner in your eyes.

275
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:42,910
Treasure.

276
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:45,097
I was driftwood floating at sea until you

277
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,886
struck me like a thunderbolt
igniting my soul.

278
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,380
A snack.

279
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,040
Oh, thank you.

280
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:53,716
Look at him falling all over himself.

281
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,720
Yeah, well, he was a lost
cause from the start.

282
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:02,817
Looks like you and I are the only
holdouts on this ship of insanity.

283
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,417
We shouldn't blame the others.

284
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,437
Their simple minds
can't resist her charge.

285
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,500
Hey, Usa!

286
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:09,490
Chopper!

287
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:18,180
What should I call you, Robin?

288
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:21,165
Or something more daring
that declares my love?

289
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:23,410
Leaving?

290
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,220
She's great!

291
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,900
With an adult charm!

292
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:32,945
She's far different than Nami!

293
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,860
This ship has charm.

294
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:42,000
Is it always this lively?

295
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,040
Yeah, it usually is.

296
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:52,100
This woman's up to something. But what?

297
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,900
What's the forecast, Navigator?

298
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:01,297
Is it smooth sailing ahead?

299
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:04,027
The wind is calm and
the weather's beautiful.

300
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:06,360
There's no problems on my end, sis.

301
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,510
How would you know?

302
00:17:07,593 --> 00:17:09,237
You haven't stopped
gawking at that jewelry.

303
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:12,400
Anji, is our snack ready? Be patient.
